WEBVTT

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:07.454
Graves at my command
have wak'd their sleepers.

00:00:07.491 --> 00:00:12.190
Op'd, and let 'em forth
by my so potent art.

00:00:12.229 --> 00:00:16.222
But this rough magic
I here abjure

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:19.565
and when I have requir'd
some Heavenly music...

00:00:19.603 --> 00:00:21.867
which even now I do...

00:00:21.905 --> 00:00:25.568
to work mine end
upon their senses

00:00:25.609 --> 00:00:28.510
that this airy charm is for

00:00:28.545 --> 00:00:31.207
I'll break my staff

00:00:31.248 --> 00:00:34.911
bury it certain fathoms
in the earth

00:00:34.985 --> 00:00:38.921
and deeper
than did ever plummet sound

00:00:39.022 --> 00:00:40.683
I'II...

00:00:40.724 --> 00:00:42.316
Captain?

00:00:42.359 --> 00:00:45.624
Sir, your attention
is wandering.

00:00:45.662 --> 00:00:47.289
Data, I can barely see you.

00:00:47.331 --> 00:00:49.891
But, sir, I am supposed
to be attempting

00:00:49.933 --> 00:00:52.128
a Neoplatonic magical rite.

00:00:52.169 --> 00:00:55.138
The darkness is appropriate
for such a ritual.

00:00:55.172 --> 00:00:57.572
Yes, but, Data, this is a play.

00:00:57.607 --> 00:01:00.201
The audience has to see you.

00:01:00.243 --> 00:01:04.339
Perhaps I have been too literal
with respect to my set design.

00:01:04.381 --> 00:01:07.509
Computer,
modify holodeck program

00:01:07.551 --> 00:01:08.848
Data seven-three.

00:01:08.885 --> 00:01:12.184
Shakespeare's The Tempest,
Act Five, Scene One.

00:01:12.222 --> 00:01:15.885
Increase torch light by 20%.

00:01:15.926 --> 00:01:17.860
There, that's much better.

00:01:17.894 --> 00:01:20.522
Now, do you want
to try it again?

00:01:20.564 --> 00:01:22.191
Yes, sir.

00:01:22.232 --> 00:01:26.760
Captain, I am not certain
I fully understand

00:01:26.803 --> 00:01:28.737
this Prospero character.

00:01:28.772 --> 00:01:32.139
I would appreciate
any insight you might have

00:01:32.175 --> 00:01:34.143
that would improve
my performance.

00:01:34.177 --> 00:01:36.873
Well, Data, Shakespeare
was witnessing

00:01:36.913 --> 00:01:41.543
the end of the Renaissance
and the birth of the modern era

00:01:41.585 --> 00:01:45.487
and Prospero
finds himself in a world

00:01:45.522 --> 00:01:47.922
where his powers
are no longer needed.

00:01:48.025 --> 00:01:50.926
So, we see him here
about to perform

00:01:51.028 --> 00:01:56.933
one final creative act before
giving up his art forever.

00:01:57.034 --> 00:02:01.061
There is certainly a tragic
aspect to the character.

00:02:01.104 --> 00:02:03.800
Yes, but there's
a certain expectancy, too

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.741
a hopefulness
about the future.

00:02:06.777 --> 00:02:10.406
You see, Shakespeare enjoyed
mixing opposites.

00:02:11.748 --> 00:02:12.874
The past and the future

00:02:12.949 --> 00:02:15.076
hope and despair...

00:02:15.118 --> 00:02:16.415
Data, what is this?

00:02:16.453 --> 00:02:18.421
Is this part of your program?

00:02:18.455 --> 00:02:20.685
No, sir.

00:02:20.724 --> 00:02:22.521
Well, what is going on?

00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:24.857
It appears to be
a steam locomotive.

00:02:24.895 --> 00:02:26.362
A train?

00:02:26.396 --> 00:02:27.886
If I am not mistaken.

00:02:27.998 --> 00:02:30.057
Computer, end program.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.227
Computer, end program!

00:03:23.053 --> 00:03:27.456
Space, the final frontier.

00:03:27.491 --> 00:03:31.325
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:03:31.361 --> 00:03:33.329
Its continuing mission...

00:03:33.363 --> 00:03:37.299
to explore strange new worlds

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:41.771
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:03:41.805 --> 00:03:46.435
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:04:44.267 --> 00:04:45.894
Captain...

00:04:46.002 --> 00:04:48.698
you are injured.

00:04:48.738 --> 00:04:49.705
Oh, yes, I know.

00:04:49.739 --> 00:04:50.706
It's all right.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:52.264
I'll get it seen to, Data.

00:04:56.947 --> 00:04:58.005
The train we encountered

00:04:58.048 --> 00:05:00.243
was from one of Dr. Crusher's
holodeck programs.

00:05:00.283 --> 00:05:02.649
It was a re-creation
of the Orient Express

00:05:02.686 --> 00:05:05.746
a train which traveled
from Paris to Istanbul

00:05:05.789 --> 00:05:08.087
from the late 19th century...

00:05:08.124 --> 00:05:10.422
Yes, yes, Data, I know
about the Orient Express

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:13.258
but what is it doing
on Prospero's island?

00:05:14.798 --> 00:05:17.096
There appears to have been
a malfunction

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:20.193
in the holodeck's database
retrieval program.

00:05:20.237 --> 00:05:23.206
The two programs somehow
temporarily linked together.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:24.673
Is it possible
that this malfunction

00:05:24.708 --> 00:05:26.369
would affect
the other holodecks as well?

00:05:26.409 --> 00:05:27.535
It is a possibility.

00:05:27.577 --> 00:05:28.635
I will need to run

00:05:28.678 --> 00:05:30.009
a full diagnostic
to be certain.

00:05:30.046 --> 00:05:31.172
Very good, Data

00:05:31.214 --> 00:05:32.977
but shut down
the other holodecks as well

00:05:33.016 --> 00:05:33.983
until you're finished

00:05:34.017 --> 00:05:35.279
just to be on the safe side.

00:05:35.318 --> 00:05:36.307
Aye, sir.

00:05:39.823 --> 00:05:44.351
I never realized that you
were interested in trains.

00:05:44.394 --> 00:05:46.692
Are you aware that at its peak

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:50.029
the Orient Express carried more
than 10,000 people a year?

00:05:50.066 --> 00:05:53.365
It isn't really the train itself
that I'm interested in.

00:05:53.403 --> 00:05:54.700
What then?

00:05:54.738 --> 00:05:56.365
It's the experience.

00:05:56.406 --> 00:06:00.035
The Orient Express
is romantic, mysterious.

00:06:00.076 --> 00:06:02.636
It's an elegant way
to see exotic places

00:06:02.679 --> 00:06:04.306
and meet fascinating people.

00:06:04.347 --> 00:06:07.316
Do you know that one time
on one trip

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:08.977
both Sigmund Freud
and Gertrude Stein

00:06:09.019 --> 00:06:11.647
just happened to be
in the same car?

00:06:11.688 --> 00:06:14.316
They ended up having dinner
together every night.

00:06:14.357 --> 00:06:16.325
I wonder what they talked about?

00:06:16.359 --> 00:06:19.328
Why don't you take a trip
yourself and find out?

00:06:19.362 --> 00:06:20.659
Riker to Picard.

00:06:20.697 --> 00:06:21.994
Picard here.

00:06:22.032 --> 00:06:24.330
All sections ready
to begin the survey, sir.

00:06:24.367 --> 00:06:25.664
Very good.
I'm on my way.

00:06:25.702 --> 00:06:26.999
Thank you.

00:06:27.037 --> 00:06:30.336
Don't forget the trip, Jean-Luc.
Think about it.

00:06:30.373 --> 00:06:34.070
You never know who you'll meet
on the Orient Express.

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:38.979
Captain's Log, Stardate 47869.2.

00:06:39.015 --> 00:06:41.711
After weathering an unexpected
magnascopic storm

00:06:41.751 --> 00:06:43.719
in the Mekorda sector

00:06:43.753 --> 00:06:47.086
we are continuing our search
for new Federation colony sites.

00:06:47.123 --> 00:06:49.091
I don't think
there's any possibility

00:06:49.125 --> 00:06:51.093
of developing sites
in this region.

00:06:51.127 --> 00:06:53.789
Most of the stars
are main sequence binaries.

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:55.798
There are no M-Class planets.

00:06:55.832 --> 00:06:58.665
Well, let's move on
to another survey region.

00:06:58.702 --> 00:07:00.636
Have stellar cartography
begin a...

00:07:01.638 --> 00:07:02.832
Mr. Data, report.

00:07:02.906 --> 00:07:05.204
The ship has moved
into warp, sir.

00:07:05.241 --> 00:07:07.209
Who gave that command?

00:07:07.243 --> 00:07:09.211
Apparently, no one.

00:07:09.245 --> 00:07:11.736
Helm and navigation controls
are not functioning.

00:07:11.781 --> 00:07:15.308
Our speed is now
warp 7.3 and holding.

00:07:15.352 --> 00:07:17.320
Picard to Engineering.

00:07:17.354 --> 00:07:18.719
Mr. La Forge, what's going on?

00:07:18.755 --> 00:07:20.814
We've lost primary helm control
on the Bridge.

00:07:20.857 --> 00:07:21.846
I don't understand it.

00:07:21.891 --> 00:07:23.518
The impulse systems
suddenly cut out

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:25.050
and the warp drive
just kicked in.

00:07:25.095 --> 00:07:27.290
Geordi, can you take the engines
off-line?

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:28.627
I'm working on it.

00:07:28.665 --> 00:07:30.292
Mr. Data, what's our heading?

00:07:30.333 --> 00:07:32.267
Bearing 187 mark 4, sir.

00:07:32.302 --> 00:07:34.566
I am unable to determine
our destination.

00:07:34.604 --> 00:07:37.971
However, we are moving away
from the Mekorda sector.

00:07:38.007 --> 00:07:40.567
Captain, the computer's locked
out all the propulsion controls.

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:42.840
I can't access
any of the overrides.

00:07:42.879 --> 00:07:44.437
If you want us to stop

00:07:44.481 --> 00:07:46.779
I'll have to do
an emergency core shutdown.

00:07:46.816 --> 00:07:49.114
That would leave us
without warp power

00:07:49.152 --> 00:07:50.779
for more than a week.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:53.152
Begin the procedure,
Mr. La Forge.

00:07:54.424 --> 00:07:56.722
We are no longer at warp, sir.

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:58.022
Impulse power has resumed.

00:07:58.061 --> 00:07:59.688
All systems show normal.

00:07:59.729 --> 00:08:01.026
Where are we?

00:08:01.064 --> 00:08:02.964
We are approximately
30 billion kilometers

00:08:02.999 --> 00:08:04.626
from our original position.

00:08:04.667 --> 00:08:05.964
Well done, Mr. La Forge.

00:08:06.002 --> 00:08:07.970
It wasn't me.

00:08:08.004 --> 00:08:11.735
I didn't have time to complete
the shutdown procedure.

00:08:11.775 --> 00:08:14.608
Well, I want an explanation,
Mr. La Forge.

00:08:14.644 --> 00:08:16.441
Picard out.

00:08:25.321 --> 00:08:27.289
Have you found anything yet?

00:08:27.323 --> 00:08:30.759
Only that we seem to have
more than one mystery here.

00:08:30.794 --> 00:08:34.093
We still don't know why
the ship jumped into warp

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:36.098
but it looks like we're lucky
that it did.

00:08:36.132 --> 00:08:38.600
There was a theta flux
distortion

00:08:38.635 --> 00:08:40.262
building up around the ship.

00:08:40.303 --> 00:08:42.271
Why didn't our sensors alert us?

00:08:42.305 --> 00:08:43.772
Well, our sensors
were never designed

00:08:43.807 --> 00:08:45.434
to detect theta flux distortions

00:08:45.475 --> 00:08:48.444
and yet, there is a record
of the distortion

00:08:48.478 --> 00:08:49.775
in our sensor log.

00:08:49.813 --> 00:08:51.440
That's the other mystery.

00:08:51.481 --> 00:08:53.108
One fact is clear however.

00:08:53.149 --> 00:08:55.117
The distortion was
growing in strength.

00:08:55.151 --> 00:08:56.675
If we had remained

00:08:56.719 --> 00:08:59.882
at our original position
1.7 seconds longer

00:08:59.956 --> 00:09:02.186
the distortion would have
ruptured our warp core.

00:09:02.225 --> 00:09:04.750
If the Enterprise hadn't
jumped into warp when it did

00:09:04.794 --> 00:09:06.455
we would have been
blown to pieces.

00:09:27.181 --> 00:09:28.671
I don't get it, Data.

00:09:28.716 --> 00:09:32.743
What would cause the engines
to suddenly jump into warp?

00:09:32.787 --> 00:09:35.187
Perhaps the engines
were activated

00:09:35.223 --> 00:09:37.350
by a random power fluctuation.

00:09:37.392 --> 00:09:40.691
Which occurred
just in time to save the ship?

00:09:40.728 --> 00:09:43.356
It is improbable,
but it is possible.

00:09:43.398 --> 00:09:45.491
I don't know,
I don't think I'm ready

00:09:45.533 --> 00:09:47.091
to start believing in luck.

00:09:55.944 --> 00:09:58.742
There is another possibility.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:00.008
Yeah? What's that?

00:10:00.048 --> 00:10:02.846
The sensors
apparently detected

00:10:02.884 --> 00:10:05.978
a dangerous anomaly
that threatened the Enterprise.

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:08.079
It is possible
that they triggered

00:10:08.122 --> 00:10:10.317
a safety device
that caused the ship

00:10:10.358 --> 00:10:12.121
to avoid destruction.

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:14.025
Yeah, but there's no direct link

00:10:14.062 --> 00:10:16.530
between the warp
engines and the sensors.

00:10:20.735 --> 00:10:23.295
Whoa. What is that?

00:10:23.338 --> 00:10:25.568
It looks like some kind

00:10:25.607 --> 00:10:28.098
of new circuit node,
and it's connected

00:10:28.142 --> 00:10:31.908
to at least half a dozen points
on the sensor array.

00:10:31.946 --> 00:10:34.414
It appears to be connected
to several other systems

00:10:34.449 --> 00:10:36.576
as well, including
the warp control circuits.

00:10:36.618 --> 00:10:38.245
Well, I guess there's
a connection

00:10:38.286 --> 00:10:41.551
between the warp engines
and the sensors after all.

00:10:45.093 --> 00:10:46.253
A force field.

00:10:46.294 --> 00:10:48.387
Where did that come from?

00:10:48.429 --> 00:10:49.862
I am not certain.

00:10:49.897 --> 00:10:52.923
Perhaps it came
from the node itself.

00:10:53.001 --> 00:10:56.937
Well, wherever it came from,
it sure doesn't want us

00:10:56.971 --> 00:10:58.734
messing with this node.

00:10:58.773 --> 00:11:01.936
It appears
to be protecting itself.

00:11:04.178 --> 00:11:07.807
We found these nodes in several
systems around the ship.

00:11:07.849 --> 00:11:10.443
At some level or another,
they're all connected.

00:11:10.485 --> 00:11:13.818
These nodes were linking the
sensors to our warp control

00:11:13.855 --> 00:11:15.186
and defensive systems.

00:11:15.223 --> 00:11:17.714
We believe this is why
the ship jumped to warp.

00:11:17.759 --> 00:11:19.249
When the sensors detected danger

00:11:19.293 --> 00:11:21.284
the defensive system
reacted to the threat

00:11:21.329 --> 00:11:23.320
and activated the warp engines
to protect us.

00:11:23.364 --> 00:11:24.797
Where did the nodes come from?

00:11:24.832 --> 00:11:26.663
It is possible
the magnascopic storm

00:11:26.701 --> 00:11:29.226
we recently encountered
had an unexpected effect

00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:31.500
on the ship's systems.

00:11:31.539 --> 00:11:33.905
Wherever they come from,
they seem to be multiplying.

00:11:33.941 --> 00:11:35.340
As they increase, it will become

00:11:35.376 --> 00:11:38.743
progressively more difficult
to control the ship.

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:40.042
What do you propose we do?

00:11:40.081 --> 00:11:42.572
Well, getting rid of them
isn't going to be so easy.

00:11:42.617 --> 00:11:44.642
When we attempted
to examine the circuitry

00:11:44.686 --> 00:11:46.916
of one of the nodes,
it generated a force field

00:11:47.021 --> 00:11:49.353
to keep us out.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:52.450
Well, whatever's going on,
our first priority

00:11:52.493 --> 00:11:54.927
is getting back
control of the ship.

00:11:54.962 --> 00:11:57.396
Agreed.
All of the nodal connections

00:11:57.432 --> 00:11:59.332
intersect in Holodeck Three.

00:11:59.367 --> 00:12:02.268
It appears to be a focal point
of some kind.

00:12:02.303 --> 00:12:05.272
We might be able to find a way
to use the holodeck's circuitry

00:12:05.306 --> 00:12:06.898
to disable the nodes
permanently.

00:12:07.942 --> 00:12:09.637
All right, let's do it.

00:12:15.249 --> 00:12:18.582
Commander, the holodeck
appears to be in operation.

00:12:18.619 --> 00:12:21.349
I thought you shut down
the entire system.

00:12:21.389 --> 00:12:23.721
I did, but it
has reactivated itself

00:12:23.758 --> 00:12:25.282
and it will not disengage.

00:12:25.326 --> 00:12:26.987
Which program is running?

00:12:27.028 --> 00:12:30.589
Several different programs
are running simultaneously.

00:12:30.631 --> 00:12:32.622
This should be interesting.

00:13:34.028 --> 00:13:36.292
You weren't kidding, Mr. Data.

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:37.854
No, sir.

00:13:37.899 --> 00:13:41.528
I estimate that this... scene
consists of portions

00:13:41.569 --> 00:13:44.197
of seven distinct
holodeck programs.

00:13:44.238 --> 00:13:46.729
See if you can
access the circuits

00:13:46.774 --> 00:13:49.538
that have been
affected by the nodes.

00:14:08.262 --> 00:14:12.130
Tickets.
Tickets, please.

00:14:12.166 --> 00:14:14.396
Please have your tickets ready.

00:14:14.435 --> 00:14:15.732
Thank you, sir.

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:17.067
Thank you, madam.

00:14:17.104 --> 00:14:18.162
There you are.

00:14:18.206 --> 00:14:19.730
Thank you.

00:14:19.774 --> 00:14:21.765
Thank you, sir.

00:14:21.809 --> 00:14:23.572
Tickets, please.

00:14:23.611 --> 00:14:26.603
You know, I never even
been away from home.

00:14:26.647 --> 00:14:29.707
Now I'm going all the way
to Vertiform City.

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:30.808
Very nice, sir.

00:14:30.852 --> 00:14:31.978
Enjoy your trip.

00:14:32.019 --> 00:14:33.714
Tickets, please.
Tickets?

00:14:33.754 --> 00:14:34.846
Thank you, sir.

00:14:34.889 --> 00:14:36.982
Tickets, please.

00:14:37.024 --> 00:14:39.390
Tickets, please.

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:44.327
Commander?

00:14:44.365 --> 00:14:45.696
Tickets.

00:14:46.868 --> 00:14:49.359
I've located a large
concentration of nodes

00:14:49.403 --> 00:14:50.461
behind this wall.

00:14:50.504 --> 00:14:52.665
They appear
to be connected directly

00:14:52.707 --> 00:14:55.005
to the holodeck's
main power coupling.

00:14:55.042 --> 00:14:57.067
All right, go ahead
and depolarize

00:14:57.111 --> 00:14:58.476
the entire power grid.

00:14:58.512 --> 00:15:01.504
The power grid is located
beneath this deck, sir.

00:15:01.549 --> 00:15:03.744
Get away from there!

00:15:03.784 --> 00:15:06.651
Would you gentlemen care
to show me your tickets?

00:15:09.056 --> 00:15:12.548
I believe we left our tickets
in our compartments.

00:15:12.593 --> 00:15:15.619
Mr. Worf, I told you
to bring the tickets.

00:15:15.663 --> 00:15:18.131
I, uh, forgot.

00:15:18.165 --> 00:15:21.566
I don't think you folks
belong on this train.

00:15:23.037 --> 00:15:24.470
Hold it!

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:28.105
You leave these people alone.

00:15:28.142 --> 00:15:30.007
They're only trying to help.

00:15:31.279 --> 00:15:33.304
You go back to the engine.

00:15:33.347 --> 00:15:35.440
This doesn't concern you.

00:15:35.483 --> 00:15:38.452
They're all trying
to hijack the train.

00:15:38.486 --> 00:15:40.511
Hey, if you're the engineer

00:15:40.554 --> 00:15:42.215
who's doing the driving?

00:15:51.799 --> 00:15:53.699
I am.

00:16:00.775 --> 00:16:03.539
Easy, sir. Easy.
I got you.

00:16:03.577 --> 00:16:06.341
I'm all right.
Thanks.

00:16:08.649 --> 00:16:12.050
Looks like the navigational
relay's overloaded.

00:16:25.166 --> 00:16:27.157
Geordi, what's going on?

00:16:27.201 --> 00:16:28.691
We just went into warp.

00:16:28.736 --> 00:16:31.864
We've lost engine
and helm control again, Captain

00:16:31.906 --> 00:16:34.739
but this time...
they're completely burned out.

00:16:34.775 --> 00:16:37.141
I don't know
if we can stop the ship.

00:16:37.178 --> 00:16:40.579
I believe
we have changed direction.

00:16:40.614 --> 00:16:43.139
Now we're on the right track.

00:16:43.184 --> 00:16:46.745
Ladies and gentlemen,
we are on our way.

00:16:57.164 --> 00:16:58.495
I was right.

00:16:58.532 --> 00:17:00.898
He was trying
to make off with my brick.

00:17:01.002 --> 00:17:02.970
Take good care of that.

00:17:03.004 --> 00:17:05.370
We can't afford to lose it.

00:17:07.541 --> 00:17:09.372
Now, are you people
going to leave

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:11.708
or do we have
to throw you off the train?

00:17:11.746 --> 00:17:13.373
Commander.

00:17:17.885 --> 00:17:19.614
According to my tricorder

00:17:19.653 --> 00:17:22.747
the holodeck safeties
have been disengaged.

00:17:22.790 --> 00:17:24.257
His weapon could be lethal.

00:17:24.291 --> 00:17:26.919
All right,
let's get out of here.

00:17:43.677 --> 00:17:46.737
The number of systems
now being affected by the nodes

00:17:46.781 --> 00:17:48.373
has increased considerably.

00:17:48.416 --> 00:17:50.884
Sensors, engines,
replicators, propulsion...

00:17:50.951 --> 00:17:52.782
they're all
working together now

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:55.186
almost independently
of the main computer

00:17:55.222 --> 00:17:57.850
and the nodes link them all
through the holodeck.

00:17:57.892 --> 00:17:59.120
But why the holodeck?

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:00.388
It doesn't make any sense.

00:18:00.428 --> 00:18:03.022
Commander, I believe
what happens on the holodeck

00:18:03.064 --> 00:18:04.929
has a direct effect on the ship.

00:18:04.965 --> 00:18:07.195
When we attempted
to destroy the nodes

00:18:07.234 --> 00:18:10.203
the characters on the train
responded almost immediately

00:18:10.237 --> 00:18:11.636
to stop us.

00:18:14.708 --> 00:18:17.142
And when the engineer
tried to protect us

00:18:17.178 --> 00:18:19.373
one of the other characters
shot him.

00:18:19.413 --> 00:18:20.437
Then the conductor

00:18:20.481 --> 00:18:22.972
signaled for the train
to change direction

00:18:23.017 --> 00:18:24.678
and, at approximately
the same time...

00:18:24.718 --> 00:18:26.845
The Enterprise also took off
in a new direction.

00:18:26.921 --> 00:18:30.084
Are you saying the ship is
under control of the holodeck?

00:18:30.124 --> 00:18:31.489
Not precisely.

00:18:31.525 --> 00:18:34.494
Geordi, does the configuration
of connection nodes

00:18:34.528 --> 00:18:35.790
Iook familiar to you?

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:38.765
Yeah.

00:18:38.799 --> 00:18:41.290
Yeah, it looks a little
like the structure

00:18:41.335 --> 00:18:42.563
of your positronic brain.

00:18:42.603 --> 00:18:43.627
That is correct.

00:18:43.671 --> 00:18:45.434
It would appear that the nodes

00:18:45.473 --> 00:18:48.874
are in the process of creating
a rudimentary neural net.

00:18:48.943 --> 00:18:52.344
Data, what are you suggesting?

00:18:52.379 --> 00:18:54.108
Unlikely as it may sound

00:18:54.148 --> 00:18:58.642
I believe the Enterprise
may be forming an intelligence.

00:19:10.731 --> 00:19:13.632
This is a synaptic map
of the human neocortex

00:19:13.667 --> 00:19:16.500
this is a cross-section
of my positronic net

00:19:16.537 --> 00:19:19.438
and this is a schematic

00:19:19.473 --> 00:19:22.533
of the connection nodes
linking the ship's systems.

00:19:22.576 --> 00:19:24.942
I believe some sort
of neural matrix

00:19:24.978 --> 00:19:26.240
is forming on the ship.

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:28.009
It is still relatively primitive

00:19:28.048 --> 00:19:29.811
but it is an intelligence,
nonetheless.

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:31.408
How could that happen?

00:19:31.451 --> 00:19:33.578
I believe it is
an emergent property.

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:34.814
Explain.

00:19:34.855 --> 00:19:37.517
Complex systems
can sometimes behave in ways

00:19:37.558 --> 00:19:39.526
that are entirely unpredictable.

00:19:39.560 --> 00:19:41.289
The human brain, for example

00:19:41.328 --> 00:19:44.297
might be described
in terms of cellular functions

00:19:44.331 --> 00:19:46.322
and neurochemical interactions.

00:19:46.366 --> 00:19:47.856
But that description

00:19:47.968 --> 00:19:51.529
does not explain
human consciousness

00:19:51.572 --> 00:19:54.871
a capacity that far exceeds
simple neural functions.

00:19:54.942 --> 00:19:58.878
Consciousness
is an emergent property.

00:19:58.946 --> 00:19:59.878
In other words, something

00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:01.538
that's more than just
the sum of its parts.

00:20:01.582 --> 00:20:02.606
Exactly.

00:20:02.649 --> 00:20:03.775
How does that explain

00:20:03.817 --> 00:20:05.785
what's happening
to the Enterprise?

00:20:05.819 --> 00:20:07.446
The Enterprise contains

00:20:07.487 --> 00:20:10.820
a vast database of information
which is managed

00:20:10.857 --> 00:20:12.449
by a sophisticated computer.

00:20:12.492 --> 00:20:13.618
This complex system

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:15.821
gives the ship
many of the characteristics

00:20:15.862 --> 00:20:17.489
of a biological organism.

00:20:17.531 --> 00:20:19.556
That's true...
it sees with its sensors

00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:22.194
and it talks
with its communications systems.

00:20:22.235 --> 00:20:26.399
In a sense, it almost reproduces
with the replicators.

00:20:26.440 --> 00:20:27.702
And you think that the ship

00:20:27.741 --> 00:20:29.606
has somehow
gone beyond these functions.

00:20:29.643 --> 00:20:31.133
It's developing a new capacity.

00:20:31.178 --> 00:20:32.475
Yes, sir, I believe

00:20:32.512 --> 00:20:35.538
a self-determining
intelligence is emerging.

00:20:35.582 --> 00:20:38.676
If that is so, what does
the ship want?

00:20:38.719 --> 00:20:40.152
Where is it taking us?

00:20:40.187 --> 00:20:41.279
I believe the key

00:20:41.321 --> 00:20:43.516
to understanding
the ship's behavior

00:20:43.557 --> 00:20:44.922
lies in the holodeck.

00:20:44.992 --> 00:20:48.428
All of the connection nodes
intersect at that location.

00:20:48.462 --> 00:20:50.760
It is clearly some kind
of processing center.

00:20:50.797 --> 00:20:52.321
Processing center?

00:20:52.366 --> 00:20:53.924
Yes, sir.
A focal point

00:20:54.034 --> 00:20:56.229
where all the ideas
and instincts

00:20:56.269 --> 00:20:58.294
of this emerging intelligence

00:20:58.338 --> 00:21:00.568
are first expressed
in some form.

00:21:00.607 --> 00:21:02.541
Almost like an imagination.

00:21:02.576 --> 00:21:05.545
Captain, I'd like
to go to the holodeck.

00:21:05.579 --> 00:21:07.809
I could interact
with the characters

00:21:07.848 --> 00:21:09.372
and maybe find some clues

00:21:09.416 --> 00:21:12.010
to help us understand
what's happening.

00:21:12.052 --> 00:21:13.417
Very well.

00:21:13.453 --> 00:21:15.250
Mr. Data, Mr. Worf,
I want you to go along.

00:21:15.288 --> 00:21:17.779
See if you can reestablish
control of the ship

00:21:17.824 --> 00:21:20.122
without damaging the nodes.

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:23.391
If the ship is truly
an emerging intelligence

00:21:23.430 --> 00:21:25.489
then we have a responsibility

00:21:25.532 --> 00:21:29.332
to treat it with the same
respect as any other being.

00:21:45.018 --> 00:21:46.883
Welcome aboard, Counselor.

00:21:46.920 --> 00:21:50.253
If you will distract
these people

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:52.656
I will attempt to depolarize
the power grid.

00:22:04.738 --> 00:22:06.365
Excuse me.

00:22:06.406 --> 00:22:08.033
Have you finished
the puzzle yet?

00:22:08.075 --> 00:22:11.203
Not yet,
but we're getting close.

00:22:11.244 --> 00:22:14.873
Do you recognize it?

00:22:14.981 --> 00:22:17.415
No.

00:22:29.029 --> 00:22:31.554
I would like to help.

00:22:31.598 --> 00:22:33.896
Tell me, what exactly
are you making?

00:22:33.967 --> 00:22:35.867
What do you think we're making?

00:22:35.902 --> 00:22:37.369
A puzzle.

00:22:37.404 --> 00:22:38.894
No. No, I meant the picture.

00:22:39.005 --> 00:22:40.097
What is it?

00:22:40.140 --> 00:22:44.372
Well, I don't know.

00:22:44.411 --> 00:22:47.107
Can you deal me in?

00:22:47.147 --> 00:22:48.171
Sorry.

00:22:48.215 --> 00:22:50.547
It's a two-man game.

00:22:55.388 --> 00:22:56.753
Hey!

00:22:56.790 --> 00:22:58.690
Get your hand off of that.

00:22:58.725 --> 00:23:02.058
Is that why you killed
the engineer?

00:23:02.095 --> 00:23:03.653
To get this brick?

00:23:03.697 --> 00:23:04.857
I had to get it back.

00:23:04.931 --> 00:23:07.058
You know what it's worth, lady?

00:23:07.100 --> 00:23:08.465
Plenty.

00:23:08.502 --> 00:23:11.403
And I got to get it
to Keystone City.

00:23:11.438 --> 00:23:12.996
Why?
What's at Keystone City?

00:23:13.039 --> 00:23:15.564
It's where everything begins.

00:23:15.609 --> 00:23:18.476
Gin.

00:23:25.352 --> 00:23:27.786
Are you succeeding, Commander?

00:23:27.821 --> 00:23:30.881
I am ready to access
the main power grid.

00:23:30.924 --> 00:23:32.983
Keystone City, next stop.

00:23:33.026 --> 00:23:34.891
Keystone City.

00:23:34.928 --> 00:23:37.260
Well...

00:23:37.297 --> 00:23:38.889
Iook who's back.

00:23:38.965 --> 00:23:41.024
We do not want any trouble.

00:23:41.067 --> 00:23:43.467
We are simply... passengers.

00:23:43.503 --> 00:23:45.835
Well, then I'm sure
you wouldn't mind

00:23:45.872 --> 00:23:48.568
showing me your tickets.

00:23:48.608 --> 00:23:50.599
Right.

00:23:50.644 --> 00:23:52.475
Sorry, boys.

00:23:52.512 --> 00:23:54.912
You're getting off right here.

00:23:57.217 --> 00:23:58.411
This is my stop.

00:23:58.451 --> 00:23:59.577
Wait.

00:23:59.619 --> 00:24:01.348
What happens at Keystone City?

00:24:01.388 --> 00:24:03.379
Why are you taking
the brick there?

00:24:03.423 --> 00:24:05.015
Excuse me.

00:24:07.661 --> 00:24:09.856
I think we should follow
that man.

00:24:09.896 --> 00:24:12.456
That brick might be
an important clue.

00:24:45.866 --> 00:24:47.629
Where did he go?

00:24:59.779 --> 00:25:02.407
I can access
the power grid here.

00:25:07.787 --> 00:25:10.585
I will attempt
to depolarize the grid

00:25:10.624 --> 00:25:13.752
by using a low-frequency
inversion field.

00:25:13.793 --> 00:25:16.728
It may disengage the nodes
without destroying them.

00:25:18.398 --> 00:25:20.593
There he is.

00:25:20.634 --> 00:25:21.931
I'm going after him.

00:26:22.495 --> 00:26:25.555
What are you doing here?

00:26:25.598 --> 00:26:28.328
Laying the foundation.

00:26:39.145 --> 00:26:41.238
Now if youse will excuse me

00:26:41.281 --> 00:26:43.340
I got a train to catch.

00:26:54.427 --> 00:26:55.621
I don't understand it, Captain.

00:26:55.662 --> 00:26:58.460
All of a sudden, Cargo Bay Five
started to depressurize.

00:26:58.498 --> 00:26:59.897
Did everyone get out in time?

00:26:59.933 --> 00:27:02.163
Yes, sir, and I've reestablished
the containment field

00:27:02.202 --> 00:27:05.035
but I'm reading massive
power surges in the cargo bay

00:27:05.071 --> 00:27:06.663
and all sorts
of transporter activity

00:27:06.706 --> 00:27:08.640
something weird is
happening there, Captain.

00:27:08.675 --> 00:27:10.836
I want you to send a team
down there immediately.

00:27:10.877 --> 00:27:12.037
Find out what's going on.

00:27:12.078 --> 00:27:13.067
Aye, sir.

00:27:39.105 --> 00:27:40.697
La Forge to Bridge.

00:27:40.740 --> 00:27:42.207
Picard here.

00:27:42.242 --> 00:27:44.403
What's going on?

00:27:44.444 --> 00:27:46.571
I wish I could tell you.

00:28:00.158 --> 00:28:02.820
That man said he was
laying a foundation.

00:28:02.927 --> 00:28:06.419
A foundation for what?

00:28:06.464 --> 00:28:07.829
Troi to Data.

00:28:07.865 --> 00:28:09.162
Data here.

00:28:09.200 --> 00:28:10.531
How are you doing?

00:28:10.568 --> 00:28:13.093
I encountered
a minor difficulty, Counselor

00:28:13.137 --> 00:28:14.832
but it has been dealt with.

00:28:23.915 --> 00:28:27.407
I am ready to depolarize
the power grid.

00:28:31.356 --> 00:28:34.848
It looks like
the ship's replicator

00:28:34.892 --> 00:28:39.727
and transporter systems
have been merged somehow

00:28:39.764 --> 00:28:41.288
to create this.

00:28:41.332 --> 00:28:44.130
The question is, what is it?

00:28:44.168 --> 00:28:46.136
Ensign, I want you to run

00:28:46.170 --> 00:28:48.502
a full spectral analysis
on this...

00:28:52.210 --> 00:28:55.043
I'm reading massive
power fluctuations.

00:28:55.079 --> 00:28:58.344
The ship is losing
its structural integrity.

00:28:58.383 --> 00:29:00.476
What's happening?

00:29:02.420 --> 00:29:04.354
It's an earthquake.

00:29:09.894 --> 00:29:12.089
La Forge to Data.

00:29:12.130 --> 00:29:13.597
Stop what you're doing.

00:29:13.631 --> 00:29:14.757
Acknowledged.

00:29:18.936 --> 00:29:20.836
Are you all right?

00:29:20.938 --> 00:29:22.997
I'm fine.

00:29:25.777 --> 00:29:28.245
Data, I think
we ought to get together

00:29:28.279 --> 00:29:29.746
and compare notes.

00:29:29.781 --> 00:29:31.112
Agreed.

00:29:35.586 --> 00:29:38.020
The ship was
protecting itself again...

00:29:38.056 --> 00:29:39.956
stopping us from interfering.

00:29:39.991 --> 00:29:42.858
Whatever it's doing,
it intends to continue.

00:29:42.894 --> 00:29:44.828
I'm betting that all this
has something to do

00:29:44.862 --> 00:29:47.023
with that object
that's forming in the cargo bay.

00:29:47.065 --> 00:29:48.464
I think he's right, Captain.

00:29:48.499 --> 00:29:51.696
Look at the common themes
playing out on the holodeck...

00:29:51.736 --> 00:29:54.864
a puzzle being put together,
a foundation being laid

00:29:54.939 --> 00:29:56.873
a paper doll being fashioned.

00:29:56.908 --> 00:30:00.241
They're all images
of something being constructed.

00:30:00.278 --> 00:30:02.041
And some kind of object

00:30:02.080 --> 00:30:05.379
in the cargo bay that's being
constructed atom by atom.

00:30:05.416 --> 00:30:06.713
What is that object?

00:30:06.751 --> 00:30:08.616
I have no idea

00:30:08.653 --> 00:30:10.644
but it's composed
of silica polymers, duranium

00:30:10.688 --> 00:30:12.053
and a couple of other compounds

00:30:12.090 --> 00:30:13.682
we haven't been able
to identify yet.

00:30:13.725 --> 00:30:16.159
But creating it has had
quite an effect on our systems.

00:30:16.194 --> 00:30:18.992
Warp power has dropped 47%.

00:30:19.030 --> 00:30:21.828
Counselor, did you draw
any other conclusions

00:30:21.866 --> 00:30:24.198
from your experiences
on the holodeck?

00:30:24.235 --> 00:30:27.398
Anything that would help us
to understand this situation?

00:30:27.438 --> 00:30:30.373
The holodeck was full
of metaphoric imagery

00:30:30.408 --> 00:30:33.309
like it was having
some kind of daydream.

00:30:33.344 --> 00:30:35.335
It may not make literal sense

00:30:35.379 --> 00:30:38.143
but symbolically,
it probably does have

00:30:38.182 --> 00:30:40.275
some kind of logic to it.

00:30:40.318 --> 00:30:44.311
These characters you spoke to,
do they have any significance?

00:30:44.355 --> 00:30:48.018
I think they represent
different aspects of the ship.

00:30:48.059 --> 00:30:49.856
The engineer, for instance

00:30:49.894 --> 00:30:52.488
may represent
the navigational system.

00:30:52.530 --> 00:30:55.431
The gunslinger
could be the weapon system.

00:30:55.466 --> 00:30:58.026
Is there any way
that we can persuade them

00:30:58.069 --> 00:31:00.264
to give us back
control of the ship?

00:31:00.304 --> 00:31:03.762
I don't think it's possible
to reason with them.

00:31:03.808 --> 00:31:07.801
Many of them are genuinely
unaware of what's going on.

00:31:07.845 --> 00:31:10.871
It's as though
this emergent intelligence

00:31:10.915 --> 00:31:13.475
is like an infant
acting on impulse

00:31:13.518 --> 00:31:16.487
trying to figure
itself out as it goes.

00:31:16.521 --> 00:31:19.149
The only source of experience
it can draw on is ours

00:31:19.190 --> 00:31:20.680
through our holodeck programs.

00:31:20.725 --> 00:31:24.092
Then, is there a way
that we can relate to them

00:31:24.128 --> 00:31:25.425
on their own level?

00:31:25.463 --> 00:31:27.829
Find some way
to influence their behavior?

00:31:29.901 --> 00:31:32.267
Maybe there is.

00:31:32.303 --> 00:31:35.101
I'd like to go back and try.

00:31:35.139 --> 00:31:40.042
Counselor, we haven't been able
to reestablish the safeties.

00:31:40.077 --> 00:31:44.343
The injuries you suffered
on the holodeck weren't severe

00:31:44.382 --> 00:31:47.044
but next time,
they might kill you.

00:31:47.084 --> 00:31:49.052
I'm aware of that.

00:31:51.122 --> 00:31:52.589
Very well, Counselor.

00:31:52.623 --> 00:31:53.920
Go ahead.

00:31:53.958 --> 00:31:55.425
But bear in mind

00:31:55.459 --> 00:31:58.553
that whenever we have tried
to hinder their efforts

00:31:58.596 --> 00:31:59.893
we've failed.

00:31:59.931 --> 00:32:03.526
Perhaps it's time
to cooperate with them.

00:32:11.776 --> 00:32:15.268
You don't belong on this train.

00:32:15.313 --> 00:32:17.975
Three tickets
for Vertiform City.

00:32:18.015 --> 00:32:20.279
Well...

00:32:20.318 --> 00:32:23.879
I guess I was wrong
about you folks.

00:32:23.921 --> 00:32:26.185
Welcome aboard.

00:32:29.260 --> 00:32:30.557
What was that?

00:32:30.595 --> 00:32:32.893
We've been having some problems.

00:32:32.997 --> 00:32:35.693
The engine
is running out of steam.

00:32:35.733 --> 00:32:39.169
I hope we make it
to Vertiform City on time.

00:32:39.203 --> 00:32:41.228
Is there anything
we can do to help?

00:32:41.272 --> 00:32:42.569
Well, I could use

00:32:42.607 --> 00:32:45.098
a pair of strong arms
in the engine room.

00:32:45.142 --> 00:32:47.269
Might help us
get back on schedule.

00:32:47.311 --> 00:32:49.711
Why don't you go with him, Worf.

00:32:49.747 --> 00:32:52.477
We'll see what we can do here.

00:32:56.420 --> 00:32:58.081
Excuse me.

00:32:58.122 --> 00:33:00.454
Are we going to get there okay?

00:33:00.491 --> 00:33:01.788
Of course.

00:33:01.826 --> 00:33:03.851
You needn't worry about a thing.

00:33:03.961 --> 00:33:07.658
So, tell me everything
you know about Vertiform City.

00:33:07.698 --> 00:33:10.462
Well, they got this
restaurant there

00:33:10.501 --> 00:33:13.595
where you can eat
all you want, anytime.

00:33:13.638 --> 00:33:15.629
It's the best food around.

00:33:18.643 --> 00:33:22.010
There's the coal,
and there's the boiler.

00:33:22.046 --> 00:33:24.537
I'm much obliged for your help.

00:33:37.995 --> 00:33:39.462
Well done, sir.

00:33:39.497 --> 00:33:43.831
I think this will make
a big difference, all right.

00:33:50.741 --> 00:33:54.040
I don't know how or why, sir,
but warp power

00:33:54.078 --> 00:33:56.546
appears to be back
at normal levels.

00:33:56.580 --> 00:33:58.411
What's our heading?

00:33:58.449 --> 00:34:02.215
We appear to be on a course
for Tambor Beta VI.

00:34:02.253 --> 00:34:04.312
It's a white dwarf star.

00:34:05.690 --> 00:34:07.453
Keep it steady.

00:34:07.491 --> 00:34:10.085
Put your back into it.

00:34:10.127 --> 00:34:12.322
That's the ticket!

00:34:22.406 --> 00:34:25.034
The ship is using
a modified tractor beam

00:34:25.076 --> 00:34:28.045
to collect vertion
particles from the star.

00:34:28.079 --> 00:34:30.070
Vertion particles.

00:34:30.114 --> 00:34:31.775
Vertiform City...

00:34:31.816 --> 00:34:34.808
that's what the ship
was looking for.

00:34:37.321 --> 00:34:41.417
The particles are being routed
through the transporter system

00:34:41.459 --> 00:34:42.892
into Cargo Bay Five.

00:34:42.927 --> 00:34:44.451
Geordi, what's going on?

00:34:44.495 --> 00:34:47.464
The object is absorbing
vertion particles.

00:34:47.498 --> 00:34:50.467
It's growing even faster
than before.

00:34:50.501 --> 00:34:51.900
Commander...

00:34:52.003 --> 00:34:55.336
I'm picking up internal energy
from this thing.

00:34:55.373 --> 00:34:56.840
What do you mean?

00:34:56.874 --> 00:34:59.502
I mean it's generating
its own energy.

00:34:59.543 --> 00:35:01.738
I'm picking up
coherent emissions

00:35:01.779 --> 00:35:04.111
matter conversion...

00:35:04.148 --> 00:35:05.445
it's incredible.

00:35:05.483 --> 00:35:06.950
Wait a minute.

00:35:06.984 --> 00:35:09.179
Wait a minute.
Something's wrong.

00:35:09.220 --> 00:35:11.188
We've got power fluctuations.

00:35:11.222 --> 00:35:13.656
Vertion absorption rate
is dropping.

00:35:13.691 --> 00:35:16.387
What's happening
with the particle beam?

00:35:16.427 --> 00:35:20.295
The beam's exhausted the supply
of particles in the star.

00:35:20.331 --> 00:35:22.526
There's nothing left
to take out.

00:35:22.566 --> 00:35:25.797
Captain, the energy output
of the object is decreasing.

00:35:25.836 --> 00:35:28.270
Something's wrong.

00:35:28.305 --> 00:35:30.273
What is it?

00:35:30.307 --> 00:35:35.108
This was supposed
to be Vertiform City.

00:35:44.388 --> 00:35:49.155
We've been on
the wrong track all along.

00:36:07.044 --> 00:36:08.443
Are you all right?

00:36:08.479 --> 00:36:09.969
Yes. What happened?

00:36:10.014 --> 00:36:12.676
The conductor accidentally
derailed the train.

00:36:12.717 --> 00:36:14.241
Data to Captain Picard.

00:36:14.285 --> 00:36:15.411
Picard here.

00:36:15.453 --> 00:36:17.819
There's been an accident
in the holodeck, sir.

00:36:17.855 --> 00:36:20.153
Has anything happened
on the Enterprise?

00:36:20.191 --> 00:36:22.250
Yes. We've had
a ship-wide shutdown.

00:36:22.293 --> 00:36:23.851
We've lost attitude control

00:36:23.928 --> 00:36:25.725
and most systems are off-line.

00:36:25.763 --> 00:36:28.254
Captain, you'd better
take a look at this.

00:36:28.299 --> 00:36:30.062
When the particle beam
cut off

00:36:30.101 --> 00:36:33.593
the object was beginning to form
a coherent energy matrix.

00:36:33.638 --> 00:36:35.503
Now, if these readings
are accurate

00:36:35.540 --> 00:36:38.737
I'd say that the emission
patterns were almost organic.

00:36:38.776 --> 00:36:40.437
Are you suggesting that
the Enterprise

00:36:40.478 --> 00:36:41.877
is trying to create a life-form?

00:36:41.979 --> 00:36:42.877
I think so.

00:36:42.980 --> 00:36:44.311
Will it survive?

00:36:44.348 --> 00:36:46.873
Well, its energy levels
are dropping rapidly.

00:36:46.984 --> 00:36:50.420
Unless it gets an infusion
of vertion particles...

00:36:50.454 --> 00:36:53.252
and I mean soon...
I don't think so.

00:36:59.330 --> 00:37:02.561
Captain, all of our systems
are back on line.

00:37:02.600 --> 00:37:05.034
We're moving again...
at warp nine.

00:37:05.069 --> 00:37:08.095
Let's get back to the Bridge.

00:37:13.544 --> 00:37:14.841
Whoo-ee.

00:37:14.912 --> 00:37:16.504
That was a close one, wasn't it?

00:37:16.547 --> 00:37:17.980
Where are we going now?

00:37:18.015 --> 00:37:19.846
Well, New Vertiform City,
of course.

00:37:19.917 --> 00:37:20.849
Data to Captain.

00:37:20.952 --> 00:37:22.044
Picard here.

00:37:22.086 --> 00:37:24.316
The train has returned
to normal, sir.

00:37:24.355 --> 00:37:26.619
Our destination
is New Vertiform City.

00:37:26.657 --> 00:37:27.851
What's our course?

00:37:27.925 --> 00:37:30.257
We're headed
for the Cordannas system.

00:37:30.294 --> 00:37:31.852
Another white dwarf star.

00:37:31.896 --> 00:37:34.490
It's the nearest one
to our last position.

00:37:34.532 --> 00:37:35.590
Captain...

00:37:35.633 --> 00:37:37.225
we have a problem.

00:37:37.268 --> 00:37:40.260
Even at warp nine
the Cordannas system

00:37:40.304 --> 00:37:42.864
is over 12 hours from here.

00:37:42.907 --> 00:37:46.536
Will the object in the cargo bay
survive that long?

00:37:46.577 --> 00:37:48.204
Yes, sir,
but that's not the problem.

00:37:48.246 --> 00:37:50.077
The ship has diverted
all of our systems

00:37:50.114 --> 00:37:52.207
to maximum propulsion,
including life support.

00:37:52.250 --> 00:37:54.878
We have less than two hours
of reserve oxygen.

00:37:54.986 --> 00:37:57.386
Mr. Data, we have to stop
the Enterprise.

00:37:57.421 --> 00:37:59.582
That means you have to get
control of the train.

00:37:59.624 --> 00:38:00.784
Understood, sir.

00:38:00.825 --> 00:38:03.055
The ship is looking
for vertion particles.

00:38:03.094 --> 00:38:05.085
And it believes
that the Cordannas system

00:38:05.129 --> 00:38:06.221
is the closest source.

00:38:06.264 --> 00:38:08.824
Is there any possibility
of anything closer?

00:38:08.900 --> 00:38:12.529
White dwarf stars are the only
natural sources of vertion, sir.

00:38:12.570 --> 00:38:14.094
Then what about artificial ones?

00:38:14.138 --> 00:38:15.833
Can you create the particles?

00:38:17.942 --> 00:38:20.103
How did the conductor
stop the train?

00:38:20.144 --> 00:38:22.738
There is a braking lever
in the engine room.

00:38:22.780 --> 00:38:23.747
Let's go.

00:38:23.781 --> 00:38:24.839
Sorry, folks

00:38:24.949 --> 00:38:26.940
but you ain't going nowhere.

00:38:31.188 --> 00:38:33.986
I've narrowed the search down
to the MacPherson Nebula

00:38:34.025 --> 00:38:35.219
which is a supernova remnant

00:38:35.259 --> 00:38:37.693
and Dikon alpha,
which is a class-9 pulsar.

00:38:37.728 --> 00:38:40.060
They're both fairly close
to our current flight path

00:38:40.097 --> 00:38:42.292
and either one could produce
vertion particles

00:38:42.333 --> 00:38:44.858
if we detonated a modified
photon torpedo inside it.

00:38:44.902 --> 00:38:46.802
Vertions usually occur
in minuscule amounts.

00:38:46.837 --> 00:38:48.498
Do you think either
of these phenomena

00:38:48.539 --> 00:38:49.801
could produce enough of them?

00:38:49.840 --> 00:38:51.137
It's really hard to say.

00:38:51.175 --> 00:38:53.405
I can't even guarantee
that we can create them at all.

00:38:53.444 --> 00:38:55.071
Well, we've got
to give it a try.

00:38:55.112 --> 00:38:56.739
The nebula or the pulsar?

00:38:56.781 --> 00:38:58.874
It's your choice, Mr. La Forge.

00:38:58.916 --> 00:39:01.077
I say go with the nebula.

00:39:01.118 --> 00:39:04.315
Very well.
Begin the torpedo modifications.

00:39:04.355 --> 00:39:06.186
Now let's see if we
can get this ship

00:39:06.223 --> 00:39:07.281
to go where we want.

00:39:10.361 --> 00:39:11.726
Please, listen to me.

00:39:11.762 --> 00:39:13.696
We understand what's happening.

00:39:13.731 --> 00:39:16.495
We know you have to get
to New Vertiform City

00:39:16.534 --> 00:39:18.627
and we want to help you
get there.

00:39:18.669 --> 00:39:19.966
Well, I don't know.

00:39:20.004 --> 00:39:21.096
Please.

00:39:21.138 --> 00:39:22.298
We're your friends.

00:39:22.340 --> 00:39:25.707
You really going to help us get
to New Vertiform City?

00:39:25.743 --> 00:39:27.233
I promise.

00:39:27.278 --> 00:39:30.577
Well, okay, but just one of you.

00:39:30.614 --> 00:39:32.275
The rest stay here.

00:39:41.325 --> 00:39:42.758
That's far enough.

00:39:42.793 --> 00:39:44.624
Sorry to spoil your party, pal.

00:39:44.662 --> 00:39:45.993
It's nothing personal.

00:39:46.030 --> 00:39:47.964
I can get us there more quickly.

00:39:47.999 --> 00:39:49.330
I know a shorter route.

00:39:49.367 --> 00:39:50.595
Don't listen to him.

00:39:50.634 --> 00:39:51.862
He's up to something.

00:39:51.969 --> 00:39:53.197
A shorter route?

00:39:53.237 --> 00:39:55.797
Yes, if you will let me
handle the controls.

00:39:55.840 --> 00:39:57.364
Don't do it.

00:39:57.408 --> 00:39:59.205
Well...

00:39:59.243 --> 00:40:01.711
we're already behind schedule.

00:40:01.746 --> 00:40:04.772
If you can get
us there on time...

00:40:04.815 --> 00:40:07.306
All right, go on,
but no funny stuff.

00:40:07.351 --> 00:40:09.080
Data to Captain Picard.

00:40:09.120 --> 00:40:12.146
I have taken control
of the engine room.

00:40:12.189 --> 00:40:13.486
Stand by.

00:40:13.524 --> 00:40:16.015
Are we within sensor range
of the nebula?

00:40:16.060 --> 00:40:17.721
Yes, Captain, we are.

00:40:17.762 --> 00:40:21.391
Mr. Data, I need you
to slow us to impulse speed.

00:40:21.432 --> 00:40:23.627
I will attempt to do so.

00:40:23.667 --> 00:40:26.795
I hope you know
what you're doing.

00:40:45.289 --> 00:40:48.417
Are the modifications
to the torpedoes complete?

00:40:48.459 --> 00:40:50.552
Aye, sir.

00:40:50.594 --> 00:40:52.152
Launch torpedo.

00:41:01.205 --> 00:41:03.969
It's working, Captain.

00:41:04.008 --> 00:41:08.001
The reaction is producing
vertion particles.

00:41:10.848 --> 00:41:12.372
Well, what do you know?

00:41:12.416 --> 00:41:13.713
We're here!

00:41:13.751 --> 00:41:15.776
New Vertiform City.

00:41:22.893 --> 00:41:25.020
The nodes are deactivating
all over the ship.

00:41:25.062 --> 00:41:27.553
All our systems are beginning
to function normally again.

00:41:27.598 --> 00:41:29.896
Then the purpose
of the ship's intelligence

00:41:29.967 --> 00:41:32.527
was simply to bring
this life-form into being.

00:41:32.570 --> 00:41:34.060
There are some species

00:41:34.105 --> 00:41:36.471
whose sole purpose
is to reproduce.

00:41:36.507 --> 00:41:39.101
Once they finally procreate,
they die.

00:41:39.143 --> 00:41:40.405
Captain...

00:42:13.177 --> 00:42:15.270
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:42:15.312 --> 00:42:17.872
The Enterprise
is back under our control.

00:42:17.982 --> 00:42:21.110
All traces of the emergent
intelligence are gone

00:42:21.152 --> 00:42:24.644
and the object it created
has disappeared into space.

00:42:30.094 --> 00:42:31.652
Come.

00:42:33.531 --> 00:42:36.762
Captain, I am staging a scene
from The Tempest

00:42:36.800 --> 00:42:38.563
this evening
for a small audience.

00:42:38.602 --> 00:42:40.035
I would like for you to attend.

00:42:40.070 --> 00:42:41.537
I would be honored.

00:42:41.572 --> 00:42:42.903
What scene?

00:42:42.940 --> 00:42:45.602
Miranda's first encounter
with other human beings.

00:42:47.378 --> 00:42:52.475
"O brave new world,
that has such people in it."

00:42:52.516 --> 00:42:54.643
It seemed appropriate.

00:42:58.856 --> 00:43:01.689
Captain, you took
a substantial risk

00:43:01.725 --> 00:43:05.786
in allowing the Enterprise
to... complete its task.

00:43:05.829 --> 00:43:07.126
Why do you say that?

00:43:07.164 --> 00:43:09.860
Because the end result
was unknown.

00:43:09.967 --> 00:43:12.299
The object
could have been dangerous.

00:43:12.336 --> 00:43:14.600
It may, in fact, be dangerous.

00:43:14.638 --> 00:43:17.766
And I have allowed it to go off
on its merry way.

00:43:17.808 --> 00:43:19.070
Yes, sir.

00:43:19.109 --> 00:43:20.508
The intelligence

00:43:20.544 --> 00:43:22.569
that was formed
on the Enterprise

00:43:22.613 --> 00:43:25.343
didn't just come out
of the ship's systems.

00:43:25.382 --> 00:43:27.873
It came from us,
from our mission records

00:43:27.985 --> 00:43:30.783
personal logs,
holodeck programs...

00:43:30.821 --> 00:43:32.118
our fantasies.

00:43:32.156 --> 00:43:35.125
Now, if our experiences
with the Enterprise

00:43:35.159 --> 00:43:36.786
have been honorable

00:43:36.827 --> 00:43:40.388
can't we trust that the sum
of those experiences

00:43:40.431 --> 00:43:42.422
will be the same?
